WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.866
One point, eight neighbours.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.913
Six numbers describe neighbour j, like distance and angle.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.289
Standardised, they form the token.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.269
Every neighbour gets one: token h sub k.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.820
The query is a matrix times the token: multiply along a row, then add.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.661
Row two gives the query's second number.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.690
Two numbers draw the query arrow.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.103
A second matrix turns every token into a key.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.053
A third makes values, kept for the next step.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.561
The score is query dot key, divided by root d.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.367
It measures the key's shadow along the query.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.976
All eight keys cast shadows, and each becomes a signed score.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.042
Key six points away: a negative score.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.502
These rank the neighbours, but they are not weights yet.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.938
A query asks, keys answer, and the dot product scores the match.
